    "long_instructions": "# Modify\r\n\r\nMuralists don’t repaint a spot that’s already painted — it wastes supplies. Extend the program with two new checks a real muralist would use before continuing their work.\r\n\r\n1. Create a variable called `ready_to_paint`, combining `is_on_paint()` and `has_paint()` with `and`. You’ll need to use `not` for one of them, so that it’s `True` only when the Painter has paint to use and the current square has no paint yet.\r\n2. Print `ready_to_paint` and check the console output.\r\n3. Create a variable called `needs_supplies`, combining `is_on_bucket()` and `has_paint()` with `or`. You’ll need to use `not` for one of them, so that it’s `True` if the Painter is standing on a bucket, or `True` if the Painter has run out of paint.\r\n4. Print `needs_supplies` and check the console output.\r\n5. Turn your painter around and move back to the bucket. Take more paint, then move one more square. Create `ready_to_paint` and `needs_supplies` again, using the same lines you wrote in steps 1 and 3, and print both.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\nprint(\"can_move():\", can_move())\nprint(\"has_paint():\", has_paint())\nmove()\ntake_paint()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\n\nready = can_move() and has_paint()\nprint(\"ready:\", ready)\n\non_something = is_on_bucket() or is_on_paint()\nprint(\"on_something:\", on_something)\nprint(\"not is_on_paint():\", not is_on_paint())\n\n# create ready_to_paint and print it\n\n# create needs_supplies and print it\n\n# turn around, move back to the bucket, take more paint, move one more square,\n\n# create ready_to_paint and needs_supplies again and print both",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "folders": {
      },
